{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "אמר אל הכהנים", :translit "emor el ha-kohanim", :gloss "say to the priests"} {:he "אוב", :translit "ov", :gloss "familiar spirit"} {:he "וידעוני", :translit "yid'oni", :gloss "wizard"} {:he "אורים ותומים", :translit "urim ve-tummim", :gloss "Urim and Thummim"} {:he "ואיש או אשה כי יהיה בהם אוב או ידעוני", :translit "ve-ish o isha ki yihyeh bahem ov o yid'oni", :gloss "and a man or woman when there is among them an ov or yid'oni"} {:he "דמיהם בם", :translit "damehem bam", :gloss "their blood is in them"} {:he "לא יטמא", :translit "lo yitama", :gloss "he shall not defile"} {:he "כהן ששמש בטומאה אחיו הכהנים מפצעים את מוחו", :translit "kohen sheshamesh be-tum'ah echav ha-kohanim mifatz'im et mocho", :gloss "a priest who served in impurity his fellow priests split his skull"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut) of Lev 21:1 to laws of ov and yid'oni in Lev 20:27"}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 20:27 prescribes capital punishment for one who inquires of an ov or yid'oni, stating 'their blood is in them' (דמיהם בם). Leviticus 21:1 opens the laws of priestly purity. The Tanḥuma (Emor §1) juxtaposes these two passages: citing Rabbi Levi, it states that Saul should have inquired through Urim veTummim rather than through the ov. A beraita in Sanhedrin 81b-b82a states that a priest who served in impurity is punished by having his skull split by fellow priests.", :sources ["Leviticus 20:27" "Leviticus 21:1" "Tanḥuma Emor 1" "Sanhedrin 81b" "1 Samuel 28:7"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אל הכהנים", :translit "el ha-kohanim", :gloss "to the priests"} {:he "לא חללים", :translit "lo chalalim", :gloss "not profaned ones"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אל הכהנים", :b "לא חללים"}], :frame {:text "The word חללים ('profaned ones') refers to priests disqualified from service. Leviticus 21:17-21 enumerates blemishes that profane a priest and disqualify him from offering bread. The gematria equating 'to the priests' with 'not profaned ones' signals that this verse addresses only valid priests.", :sources ["Leviticus 21:17" "Leviticus 21:21"]}} {:quotes [{:he "בני אהרן", :translit "bnei aharon", :gloss "sons of Aaron"} {:he "זהו", :translit "zehu", :gloss "this is it"} {:he "בעלי מומין", :translit "ba'alei mumin", :gloss "blemished ones"} {:he "בני אהרן ולא בנות אהרן", :translit "bnei aharon ve-lo benot aharon", :gloss "sons of Aaron and not daughters of Aaron"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "בני אהרן", :b "זהו"} {:kind :gematria, :a "בני אהרן", :b "בעלי מומין"}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 21:1 addresses 'the sons of Aaron,' restricting priestly defilement laws to male descendants. The gematria equating 'sons of Aaron' with 'blemished ones' (בעלי מומין) signals that the prohibition applies even to priests with disqualifying blemishes (Leviticus 21:17-23). The phrase 'stunted — death for all generations' likely refers to a beraita's classification of certain hereditary priestly lineages as permanently disqualified.", :sources ["Leviticus 21:1" "Leviticus 21:17"]}} {:quotes [{:he "אמור אל הכהנים וגו' ואמרת", :translit "emor el ha-kohanim ve-gomer ve-amarta", :gloss "say to the priests etc. and you shall say"} {:he "לדורות", :translit "le-dorot", :gloss "for generations"} {:he "ואמרת", :translit "ve-amarta", :gloss "and you shall say"} {:he "אמרו\"ת טהורות", :translit "amrut tehorot", :gloss "pure sayings"} {:he "אמירה ראשונה כדי שלא ליטמא במת", :translit "amira rishona k'dei she-lo le-itamei be-met", :gloss "first utterance so as not to defile for the dead"} {:he "אמירה שניה לטמא למת מצוה", :translit "amira shniya le-tamei le-met mitzvah", :gloss "second utterance to defile for a dead mitzvah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אמור אל הכהנים וגו' ואמרת", :b "לדורות"} {:kind :other, :note "letter rearrangement: ואמרת anagrams to אמרות טהורות"}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 21:1 contains two divine utterances: 'Say (אמור) to the priests' and 'you shall say (ואמרת) to them.' The first prohibits defilement; the second introduces the exception for close relatives. The phrase 'pure sayings' echoes Psalm 12:7, 'the sayings of the LORD are pure sayings (אמרות יהוה אמרות טהורות).' The obligation to defile for an unclaimed corpse is addressed in Mishnah Nazir 7:1.", :sources ["Leviticus 21:1" "Psalms 12:7" "Mishnah Nazir 7:1"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לנפש לא", :translit "la-nefesh lo", :gloss "for a soul/person, no"} {:he "בדם המת", :translit "be-dam ha-met", :gloss "in the blood of the dead"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "לנפש לא", :b "בדם המת"}], :frame {:text "Leviticus 21:1 states 'he shall not defile himself לנפש לא' — for the dead. Blood is identified as the essence of life and death in Leviticus 17:11: 'the blood is the life (הדם הוא הנפש).' The gematria linking 'for a soul/person — no' with 'in the blood of the dead' reinforces that the prohibition of priestly defilement centers on contact with the dead's blood.", :sources ["Leviticus 21:1" "Leviticus 17:11"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "juxtaposition (semikhut) of Lev 21:1 to laws of ov and yid'oni in Lev 20:27", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "אל הכהנים", :a-value 161, :b "לא חללים", :b-value 149, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "בני אהרן", :a-value 318, :b "זהו", :b-value 18, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "בני אהרן", :a-value 318, :b "בעלי מומין", :b-value 258, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "אמור אל הכהנים וגו' ואמרת", :a-value 1070, :b "לדורות", :b-value 646, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? false} {:kind :other, :note "letter rearrangement: ואמרת anagrams to אמרות טהורות", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :gematria, :a "לנפש לא", :a-value 491, :b "בדם המת", :b-value 491, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:24:57.607233729Z", :m